   "theory": "Exercise questions\n\n1. Choose and write the suitable answers.\n\n1) The disease of cancer occurs through uncontrolled division of the ________ of the body.\n\n(a) muscles  (b) cells  (c) bones  (d) blood\n\n2) Lung cancer was not common before ________ .\n\n(a) 1910  (b) 1920  (c) 1930  (d) 1940\n\n3) The biggest cause of lung cancer is ________ .\n\n(a) eating too much  (b) smoking  (c) not exercising  (d) obesity\n\n4) By living in ________ for a long time lung cancer too develops.\n\n(a) cities  (b) polluted air  (c) polluted water  (d) mountainous areas\n\n5) A never-ending ________ is a sign of cancer.\n\n(a) fever  (b) tiredness  (c) cough  (d) blood\n\n6) Alcohol is the name of ________ .\n\n(a) sherbet  (b) liquor  (c) juice  (d) medicine\n\n7) The use of illegal medicines to increase physical strength in sports competitions is called ________ .\n\n(a) intoxicants  (b) stamina  (c) doping  (d) physiotherapy\n\n2. Write the answers to the following questions.\n\ni. What is cancer?\n\nii. State the symptoms of lung cancer in detail.\n\niii. State the causes and symptoms of heart diseases.\n\niv. State precautionary measures to avoid heart diseases.",
