     "text": "In this way, if the walls of the heart are examined, the walls of the heart appear to consist of three layers. The outer layer is called the pericardium (Pericardium), the middle layer the myocardium (Myocardium) and in this way the inner layer the endocardium (Endocardium). From the membrane of the outer layer a special kind of fluid comes out, which is called pericardial fluid (Pericardial Fluid), because of which the movement of the heart takes place easily.",
