   "theory": "… and protects from different kinds of diseases. In one cubic millimetre of blood there are from 4 thousand up to 11 thousand of these, and their age is from a few days to a few weeks.\n\n3. Blood Platelets\n\nThese are the third kind of cells of blood. Their number in one cubic millimetre of blood is from two and a half lakh to five lakh, and its important work is the clotting of blood (Blood clotting).\n\nKinds of blood circulation\n\nBlood circulates in the body in the following ways.\n\n1. Pulmonary Circulation\n\nIn this circulation, when impure blood reaches the right atrium, from here it comes through the tricuspid valve into the right ventricle. When the right ventricle contracts, this blood goes through the right and left arteries into the lungs. Through the very fine tubes of blood, the capillaries, in the air sacs (Alveoli) present in lakhs in the lungs, the blood takes carbon dioxide and oxygen mixes into the blood. After obtaining oxygen the blood, becoming pure, comes through the veins of the lungs into the left atrium of the heart. From the left atrium of the heart the pure blood comes down through the bicuspid valve into the left ventricle. Here this pure blood becomes ready to be supplied to the whole body. This circulation is called pulmonary circulation (Pulmonary Circulation).",
