   "theory": "Effects of doping and alcohol on players\n\nTemporarily fatigue is not felt; rather performance increases immediately.\n\nThey affect the physical system of players.\n\nThey create mental anxiety, because of which attention is not concentrated.\n\nThey create breathing troubles, because of which the player gets tired in a few minutes and starts to get out of breath.\n\nThey create a shortage in the blood, which affects the health of players.\n\nThe attitude of players becomes negative, which affects performance.\n\nMethod of prevention and awareness campaign\n\nPlayers should be made aware of its negative effects.\n\nPlayers should be made acquainted with its effects on health and performance.\n\nIn free time players should be given alternative activities.\n\nPlayers should be made to practise increasing performance and achieving targets.\n\nSeminars should be arranged on alcohol and doping.\n\nA walk should be organised to avoid the harmful effects of alcohol and doping.\n\nSome event should be organised against the negative effects of alcohol.\n\nA publicity campaign should be run on the harmful effects of alcohol.\n\nThrough print and electronic media the harmful effects of alcohol should be highlighted.",
