   "content": "<p>Effects of doping and alcohol on players</p><p>Temporarily fatigue is not felt; rather performance increases immediately.</p><p>They affect the physical system of players.</p><p>They create mental anxiety, because of which attention is not concentrated.</p><p>They create breathing troubles, because of which the player gets tired in a few minutes and starts to get out of breath.</p><p>They create a shortage in the blood, which affects the health of players.</p><p>The attitude of players becomes negative, which affects performance.</p><p>Method of prevention and awareness campaign</p><p>Players should be made aware of its negative effects.</p><p>Players should be made acquainted with its effects on health and performance.</p><p>In free time players should be given alternative activities.</p><p>Players should be made to practise increasing performance and achieving targets.</p><p>Seminars should be arranged on alcohol and doping.</p><p>A walk should be organised to avoid the harmful effects of alcohol and doping.</p><p>Some event should be organised against the negative effects of alcohol.</p><p>A publicity campaign should be run on the harmful effects of alcohol.</p><p>Through print and electronic media the harmful effects of alcohol should be highlighted.</p>",
