   "content": "<p>Work that gives flame or heat</p><p>From this work there is a fear of fire through heat, sparks and the rising of flames, e.g. welding, grinding work etc. This work is dangerous. They should be kept under strict control.</p><p>Do this work only in that case when there is no alternative to it.</p><p>It should be certain that those working on heat are aware of its method and control.</p><p>Fire-resistant clothes should be used.</p><p>Work with responsibility.</p><p>It should be checked and supervised as a routine.</p><p>Things that are removed should be taken to a safe place.</p><p>Things that catch fire should be removed with safety.</p><p>There should be separate staff whose responsibility relates only to fire.</p><p>The workplace should be kept clean and safe.</p><p>After completing the work it should certainly be checked a last time, and it should also be checked one hour after completing the work.</p><p>Protection / safety from electricity</p><p>The design, installation, construction and repair of all electrical installations and appliances should be safe and away from danger.</p><p>The repair and installation of electrical appliances should be done by an expert electrician.</p><p>Electrical appliances and wiring should be protected from gnawing animals.</p><p>Electrical appliances should be checked and the defect of the appliances should be eliminated.</p>",
