   "content": "<p>Do not let the pulse become slow.</p><p>Take him immediately to a hospital or to a doctor.</p><p>Stoppage of breathing</p><p>Because of shortage of oxygen in the air, leakage of gas in closed rooms or more smoke, breathing can stop, because of which there is danger of life being lost. For it the following protective measures and first aid are given.</p><p>Certainly keep some way or other for the exit of gas in the room.</p><p>In case of smoke use a mask.</p><p>Go towards an open and airy place.</p><p>If breathing starts to stop, give him first aid immediately.</p><p>Medical aid</p><p>Keep the patient away from the crowd and lay him in the open air.</p><p>Give courage to the patient.</p><p>Try to deliver oxygen to the brain.</p><p>Artificial respiration should be given.</p>",
