   "theory": "Verbal violence means the use of improper words against someone, and such words as are unpleasant for others and hurt them or from which provocation spreads, for example:\n\nCalling by bad names.\n\nThreatening.\n\nSpreading rumours.\n\nSlandering.\n\nMocking.\n\nAbusing.\n\nLying and misstatement.\n\nProvoking.\n\nPresenting the matter of someone’s home in a wrong manner.\n\nWriting wrong messages or nonsense on the mobile phone.\n\nAll these acts come in the category of verbal violence, from which the matter can reach provocation and quarrel, and its results can also be dangerous.\n\nIndividual violence\n\nEvery human wants that in society he be seen with respect. Some powerful people try to forcibly suppress others on the strength of power, or try to dominate them, or try to adopt negative behaviour and tricks against other individuals so that they can keep their awe and authority established.\n\nThrough this he hurts others.",
