   "theory": "ii. Pivot Pass\n\nIn the pivot pass the ball is passed by turning on one foot. In this method one foot remains with the ground. Since in this action force is also applied on the ball while turning quickly, therefore the principle of balance applies here.\n\nPassing the ball through the ring\n\nThe player, while scoring, passes the ball through the ring. With one hand or with both hands, with the help of the wrists, the ball is thrown towards the ring. During this action, determining the direction and keeping the distance in view, force should be applied on the ball. Here the laws of motion will apply.\n\nBiomechanical principles in volleyball\n\nIn the game of volleyball the following skills are of importance; by using biomechanical principles in them performance can be increased.\n\nService (Service)\n\nLifting the ball (Digging)\n\nBoosting (Boosting)\n\nSmashing (Smashing)\n\ni. Serving\n\nIn volleyball service is of extreme importance. Attack can be made through service. Points can be obtained through good service. But weak service brings the team to a defensive position. The following are the methods of service.",
