   "theory": "Target and Field Games\n\nLong Jump\n\nRules of the long jump\n\nThe turn of players will be fixed by drawing lots.\n\nIf more than eight players take part in the competition, then every player will be given three turns, and the best 8 players will be given 3, 3 more turns. In case of equality at the eighth position the concerned players will be given 3, 3 more attempts.\n\nWhen the competition starts, players will not be allowed to use the runway for practice.\n\nBefore the competition starts, 2, 2 turns will be given for practice under the supervision of the judges.\n\nEvery player will be given the benefit of the correct attempt.\n\nEvery player will be given a chest number.\n\nEvery player will jump on his own turn.\n\nFailures\n\nIf beyond the take-off line there comes the mark of the player’s foot on the sand or plasticine (Plasticine) while running or jumping.\n\nJumping without one’s turn.\n\nJumping without the chest number.\n\nIf the player takes off from outside the right or left edge of the take-off board, whether the foot is ahead of or behind the line of the board.\n\nIf the player, after completing the jump, walks backwards in the pit.",
