   "content": "<p>1500-metre race</p><p>In the 1500-metre race every player covers the distance of 3 complete laps and one incomplete lap of 300 metres on the 400-metre standard track. The first lap will be the incomplete one of 300 metres and then three more complete laps of 400 metres. For the 300-metre incomplete lap, 100 metres are reduced from 400 metres and the starting point is put at that place. This starting line is drawn in the shape of a curve (Curve). Its method is that at the start of the second bend, where steps are given from 200 metres, there, at a distance of 8 inches from the inner line of the first lane, keeping the centre, an arc is drawn in 8 lanes at a distance of 100 metres backwards; this arc will be the starting line of the 1500-metre race. Instead of taking a start, the whole foot is used. The 1500-metre race starts from the international curve (Curve).</p><p>Rules of the 1500-metre race</p><p>i. There are no regular lanes for the 1500-metre race.</p><p>ii. The order of the lanes will be given by drawing lots.</p><p>iii. Before taking the start no player can touch the ground ahead of the start line.</p><p>iv. If some player, while running, pushes, holds or knocks down another player or becomes an obstruction in his race, he will be excluded from the competition.</p><p>v. There will be separate competitions for men and women.</p><p>vi. If in the opinion of the starter or recaller (Recaller) a false start has been taken, the recaller with a fire can call the players back to take the start again.</p>",
