   "theory": "Skills of badminton\n\nSkill of service\n\nServing high with the right hand:\n\nThe player should be standing in his service court.\n\nBoth feet of the player should be on the ground.\n\nSeeing the opposing player get ready.\n\nServing backhand\n\nThis service should be done with the backhand. Service is done by hitting the shuttle with a racket backstroke.\n\nSmashing\n\nWith whatever speed the shuttle is coming from the opposing court through the air at a height, keeping the balance of your body, bend the body slightly backwards and then take the hand back and smash the shuttle with force.\n\nRally\n\nDuring the rally care should be taken of footwork and of the reach of the opponent. The shuttle should not be hit again and again on one side only; rather the position of the opposing player should be disturbed. The shuttle should be thrown right and left, behind and in front, in the opposing court. Avoid too long a rally.\n\nIdea (placement)\n\nOne should form an idea by seeing the position of the opposing player. If he is far from the net, the shuttle should be dropped slowly near the net; if the opponent is near the net, then the shuttle should be thrown into the back zone.",
