     "text": "At a distance of 22 yards, on both sides, wickets are fixed in completely level ground. The place where the wicket is fixed is 9 inches wide. In it there are 3 stumps. On their tops bails are kept. The thickness of these stumps is uniform, and so much that the ball cannot pass between them. Their height above the ground is 28 inches. The length of the bails is about four and a half inches, and when they are placed on the stumps they should not be raised more than half an inch above. In case of strong wind, the bails can be removed with the consent of both captains and the umpire.",
