   "content": "<p>Centre circle</p><p>This is a circle of 1.80 metres radius in the middle of the court.</p><p>Three-point area</p><p>This area is outside the circle of 6.25 metres. If the ball is shot from outside this circle and is basketed correctly, three points are given, and if it is shot from inside this circle and is basketed correctly, two points are given, while for every successful free throw one point is given.</p><p>Backboard</p><p>The length of the backboard will be 1.80 metres, breadth 1.05 metres and thickness 3 centimetres. A rectangle is made on the backboard. Its length is 59 centimetres and breadth 45 centimetres. The distance from the floor to the lower end of the board is 2.90 metres. The pole will be at least one metre outside the end line, and 1.20 metres ahead of the end line (towards the court).</p><p>Ring and basket</p><p>In the exact middle of the line of the lower end of the rectangle of the backboard a ring is fixed firmly. With this ring a basket made of thread is also fixed. The diameter of the ring is 45 centimetres (16 inches).</p><p>Ball</p><p>The ball will be made of leather or rubber. Its weight will be 567 grams to 650 grams. The circumference is 74 to 78 centimetres.</p><p>Time of the game</p><p>The time of the game consists of four quarters of 10, 10 minutes. After the first quarter an interval of 2 minutes will be given. After half time an interval of 5 minutes will be given. At the end of the match time, if the score is equal, an extra five minutes will be given.</p>",
