   "content": "<p>The ball will be given to the opponent of the team that last touched the ball.</p><p>The throw-in will be given from the same place where the ball crossed the line.</p><p>The ball will have to be thrown in to the centre within 3 seconds.</p><p>A player cannot throw in by running.</p><p>Players should throw the ball keeping a distance of 3 metres while making the throw-in.</p><p>Touching or crossing the line while making the throw-in is a foul.</p><p>A player making a throw-in of the ball without the whistle is a foul.</p><p>Until the ball leaves the hands the player will not enter the court.</p><p>The player will have to throw in from the line of his own particular area.</p><p>Before the throw-in the player should pause slightly.</p><p>Penalty</p><p>In case of violation a throw-in will be given to the opposing team.</p><p>Throw up</p><p>In the following cases play will be restarted with a “throw up”.</p><p>When two players are victims of some irregularity at the same time.</p><p>The throw-up is given at that time when two opposing players hold the ball firmly at the same time.</p><p>Two opposing players at the same time hit the ball with their hands and throw it outside the court.</p><p>The umpire cannot decide on some double error.</p><p>Two opposing players collide at one place and at one and the same time.</p>",
